# 2026-11-27:
# * The font lookup is simpler.
#   The preferred font is looked up as font files named after its fonts,
#   such as `<PostScript name>.otf` or `.ttf`, in the folder of the option
#   `<package>.font_path` and, on Windows, of the fonts installed for the current user,
#   and loaded from them by path, with the faces that its options name.
#   Otherwise, it is used by name if `fc-list` lists all its fonts.
#   A font named in the document or in the option `<package>.mainfont`
#   is looked up in the same way; it is used as named if its options set `Path=`,
#   if it or a face that they name is a font file,
#   or if it is not found as font files and `fc-list` is not available.
#   A font file named with a folder counts as missing,
#   because fontspec takes its folder only from `Path=`.
#   With LuaLaTeX, a font that `fc-list` does not list is looked up with `luaotfload-tool`,
#   which also finds the fonts of the TeX installation;
#   without `luaotfload-tool`, a named font is used as named.
#   The lookup no longer uses the systemfonts package or kpsewhich,
#   searches the font folders of Linux and macOS, reads the names of fonts
#   from their files, or takes faces that the options do not name from the family.
#   `<<indiedown_path>>` in `default.yaml` is replaced before the YAML is read again,
#   and the font options are no longer split at commas.
# * `expect_pdf_snapshot()` draws the text of plots with showtext
#   in the fonts that the template bundles,
#   so that the snapshots do not depend on the fonts of the system.
#   The font files are matched to the faces by the style in their file names,
#   the faces are taken from one family,
#   and without bundled fonts the default font of sysfonts is used.
#   Each call registers its fonts anew and undoes the registration when it returns.
#   Regular documents are not affected: no template sets a graphics device.
# * The snapshot helpers need the packages showtext and sysfonts.
#   When updating this file, add them to `Suggests:` of the template package:
#   R CMD check warns about an undeclared sysfonts otherwise,
#   and the PDF snapshot tests are skipped where they are not installed.
# * `apply_default_yaml()` reads `header-includes` from its `metadata` argument,
#   the metadata after knitting, instead of from `rmarkdown::metadata`:
#   inline R code in `header-includes` is evaluated
#   instead of reaching LaTeX verbatim.
# * `expect_pdf_snapshot()` fails if the number of pages differs
#   from the number of page snapshots,
#   instead of deleting the snapshots of surplus pages
#   or silently adding snapshots of new pages.
# * The message about a missing preferred font with several faces
